From 5aa62600a8602b72780ebdafb0e96d8562d365e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Jun 2025 15:34:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 613/913] core: arm: psci: declare return values of
 PSCI_FEATURE command

Possible return values for CPU_SUSPEND capabilities:

Bit[1]:
- 0: if the implementation uses Original Format (PSCI0.2) for the
power_state parameter.
- 1: if the implementation uses the new extended StateID Format for the
power_state parameter.

Bit[0]
 OS-initiated mode.
- 0: if the platform does not support OS-initiated mode.
- 1: if the platform supports OS-initiated mode.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 85519e5a4be14af9bedc2b939c1931227dcdacf2 core: arm: psci: declare return values of PSCI_FEATURE command]
Signed-off-by: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Icd179ab9843c169b62a5f0e10af51a2e0a0bc5de
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/501255
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/include/sm/psci.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/include/sm/psci.h b/core/arch/arm/include/sm/psci.h
index 51583bad6..9c3e8f7eb 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/include/sm/psci.h
+++ b/core/arch/arm/include/sm/psci.h
@@ -66,6 +66,11 @@
 #define PSCI_RET_DISABLED		(-8)
 #define PSCI_RET_INVALID_ADDRESS	(-9)
 
+#define PSCI_FEATURE_OSI_NOT_SUPPORTED		(0)
+#define PSCI_FEATURE_OSI_SUPPORTED		BIT32(0)
+#define PSCI_FEATURE_ORIGINAL_STATE_ID		(0)
+#define PSCI_FEATURE_EXTENDED_STATE_ID		BIT32(1)
+
 uint32_t psci_version(void);
 int psci_cpu_suspend(uint32_t power_state, uintptr_t entry,
 		     uint32_t context_id, struct sm_nsec_ctx *nsec);
